// SyncMarker records, in the data plane, that a mirror's initial upstream
// import has finished, so the data-plane push gate opens even for an empty
// (uninitialised) upstream that never produced a default branch. *coreapi.Server
// satisfies it (it resolves the placement's cluster and routes the write
// through the entiredb bridge). Called only on a StatusReady completion.
//
// The bool reports whether the placement's home cluster accepted the RPC. A
// missing data-plane row also reads as accepted, because the data-plane
// UPDATE ignores its row count. The "nothing to do" cases return false with
// a nil error: placement gone in the registry, or no data-plane bridge
// wired. The consumer then Acks and does not record the flag as landed. A
// returned error is treated as transient — the completion is Nak'd and
// retried so the flag eventually lands. Optional: a nil SyncMarker disables
// the data-plane write entirely.
type SyncMarker interface {
	MarkMirrorInitialSyncDone(ctx context.Context, id model.RepoID) (landed bool, err error)
}

// InitialSyncMarkStore is the durable record that the data plane accepted
// the initial-sync flag for a placement (ENT-2340). The consumer reads it
// before calling SyncMarker and writes it only after SyncMarker reports the
// flag landed. That order keeps the retry obligation. A status write that
// commits before the marker fails leaves the record unset, so the redelivery
// calls the marker again. CompositeStatusWriter satisfies it across both
// placement tables.
//
// Both methods are best-effort for the consumer. A read error means "not
// known to be marked", so the marker runs. On a write error the consumer
// logs and still Acks. The next completion calls the marker once more.
type InitialSyncMarkStore interface {
	InitialSyncMarked(ctx context.Context, id model.RepoID) (bool, error)
	RecordInitialSyncMarked(ctx context.Context, id model.RepoID) error
}

